<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cambridgeshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cambridgeshire is a county in the East of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambridge">Cambridge</a> as its county town. Its northern part lies in the Fens, a low-lying region drained from the 17th century onwards. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> its eastern parts bordered the lands of the Iceni.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cambridgeshire.jpg" alt="Cambridgeshire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Verbcatcher · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ely_Cathedral_from_Quanea_Drove_A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
